// Thomas swap -- the WRAPPER SEQUENCE DELTA (100% hand-authored text, zero Square-Enix bytes).
//
// This is NOT a standalone playable .seq file -- it is the splice fragment build_thomas.py inserts
// into a RUNTIME COPY of the real stock ef227/PlayerSequence.seq (fetched fresh from the user's own
// install every build, sha256-drift-guarded, NEVER committed to the repo -- exactly the
// rung2/rung3/rung4 provenance convention: "verbatim Square-Enix .seq content is never committed;
// the build script is the committable source of truth, regenerating from the install every run").
//
// build_thomas.py applies exactly TWO edits to the donor's 24-line PlayerSequence.seq, both anchored
// on its one PlaySFX line (the stock text, byte-verified: "PlaySFX: SFX=Bahamut__Full ; Reflect=True"):
//
//   1. INSERT the block below immediately BEFORE that line.
//   2. REPLACE that line itself with the same text plus " ; HideMeshes=0,1,2,...,63" appended
//      (64 comma-separated indices, generated by the build script -- not hand-typed here, to avoid
//      a miscount. Composition-lens finding: "unmatched indices are inert", so a blanket 0-63 range
//      is safe regardless of how many distinct SFXMesh keys the native Bahamut effect actually emits).
//
// Everything else in the donor's 24 lines -- the row-check step/turn threads, Message/SetupReflect,
// the REAL "LoadSFX: SFX=Bahamut__Full ; Reflect=True ; UseCamera=True" line (kept UNMODIFIED -- this
// is what arms the real native creature load + the real cinematic camera), the chant animations, the
// WaitSFXDone/ActivateReflect/step-back/Turn tail -- ships completely untouched. The EffectPoint /
// PlaySound / SetBackgroundIntensity drama (the actual "Mega-Flare" choreography) lives in the
// DONOR's OWN ef227/Sequence.seq, nested-loaded by the RESOLVED id (227, from the name
// "Bahamut__Full"), never by our folder's id (84) -- so it is never copied, never touched, and stays
// 100% the real, unmodified Bahamut cinematic (real camera cuts, real roars, real flashes; rung 4's
// own finding, PLAN.md).
//
// THIS BLOCK -- what it does: a background thread (Sync=False -- does NOT block the main thread,
// which falls straight through to the (now HideMeshes-carrying) PlaySFX line on the very next op) that
// loads, plays, and holds THIS SAME FOLDER's own id (84) as a SEPARATE SFXData -- exactly the
// composition lens's "Route A" (a second LoadSFX; two independent SFXData entries can coexist in
// sfxList with zero shared mutable state, SFXData.cs:156-181/1373-1392) and exactly rung 7's own
// proven FileList.txt/Model mechanism (ef084/FileList.txt -- reused byte-identical from
// rung7-creature/FileList.txt -- resolves "Model creature_manifest.sfxmodel", which build_thomas.py
// deploys as OUR thomas_manifest.sfxmodel, not rung 7's Iviv-clone one).
//
//   Condition=1 == 1 : a self-evidently-always-true NCalc expression (a numeric equality, not a bare
//     boolean literal -- side-steps any doubt about the parser's literal-token spelling/case; every
//     donor StartThread in this file supplies an explicit Condition, so we do too rather than assume
//     an omitted one defaults to "always run").
//   UseCamera=False  : id 84 has no native ef###.bytes payload to feed a camera plugin -- explicit,
//     so the engine's config-dependent UseCamera default (which CAN resolve true) never accidentally
//     re-arms SFXDataCamera.currentCameraEngine for an id with nothing to drive it (rung 7's own
//     documented reasoning, README.md "Design decisions").
//   SkipSequence=True (on PlaySFX) : ef084/Sequence.seq is still on disk (rung 3's leftover byte-copy
//     of the REAL Bahamut nested drama) and SFXData.LoadSFX unconditionally re-reads it on every
//     LoadSFX call regardless of the FileList.txt/JSON-mesh branch (SFXData.cs:174) -- without this,
//     it would thread in as a SECOND, parallel, duplicate-damage copy of the real EffectPoint pair.
//     Rung 7 hit this exact trap and fixed it the same way.
//   No Reflect=True on any of these four ops (unlike rung 7's own id-84 quartet): in THIS design id 84
//     is a purely cosmetic side-thread -- the REAL spell-reflection state machine is already fully and
//     correctly carried by the untouched "SF=Bahamut__Full" LoadSFX/WaitSFXLoaded/PlaySFX/WaitSFXDone
//     chain (which keeps its own Reflect=True throughout, unmodified). Tagging the cosmetic thread's
//     ops Reflect=True too would double up bookkeeping this design has no reason to touch.

StartThread: Condition=1 == 1 ; Sync=False
	LoadSFX: SFX=84 ; Char=Caster ; UseCamera=False
	WaitSFXLoaded: SFX=84
	PlaySFX: SFX=84 ; SkipSequence=True
	WaitSFXDone: SFX=84
EndThread
